rs/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'm not sure it's even a good idea to reference a \"canvas group\", unless it makes any sort of sense by other existing conventions. In my opinion, the constant could be called `CLIP_CHILDREN_GROUP` and make just as much sense, while being less repetitive.","created_at":"2025-10-08T09:05:08Z","updated_at":"2025-10-08T10:02:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111380#discussion_r2413142919","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111380","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2413142919"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111380#discussion_r2413142919"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111380"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2413142919/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":73,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2412906263,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2413389399","pull_request_review_id":3314160771,"id":2413389399,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6P2WZX","diff_hunk":"@@ -70,6 +70,7 @@ class CanvasItem : public Node {\n \t\tCLIP_CHILDREN_DISABLED,\n \t\tCLIP_CHILDREN_ONLY,\n \t\tCLIP_CHILDREN_AND_DRAW,\n+\t\tCLIP_CHILDREN_CANVASGROUP,","path":"scene/main/canvas_item.h","commit_id":"d2d9da506a487e6db949ce74169a01203d8e38ce","original_commit_id":"34d2589a6788597e823ca753915de389c1217e7e","user":{"login":"tsutsen","id":68827291,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4ODI3Mjkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68827291?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsutsen","html_url":"https://github.com/tsutsen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsutsen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsutsen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsutsen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsutsen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsutsen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsutsen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsutsen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsutsen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsutsen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> the constant could be called `CLIP_CHILDREN_GROUP` and make as much sense, while being less repetitive\r\n\r\nYeah, I think that'd be better, especially if `CanvasGroup` is to be deprecated. \r\n\r\nMy logic for the 'CanvasGroup' name suggestion was:\r\n- Users familiar with 'CanvasGroup' node would get the idea what this mode does from its name;\r\n- Users unfamiliar with 'CanvasGroup' could look up [the docs](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_canvasgroup.html).\r\n\r\nWithout `CanvasGroup` node in the editor, this name references nothing and is basically just a nod to a deprecated feature. Even [internally](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/d61cd9149aaee6195b83bc65ca5539a27d76d61f/scene/2d/canvas_group.cpp#L37), the rendering mode is called 'transparent' but not 'CanvasGroup'. \r\n\r\nSo agreed, it's better to avoid the 'CanvasGroup' name for this `ClipChildrenMode`. And I like the `Group` option.\r\n\r\n","created_at":"2025-10-08T10:26:48Z","updated_at":"2025-10-08T10:26:48Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111380#discussion_r2413389399","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111380","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2413389399"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111380#discussion_r2413389399"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111380"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2413389399/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":73,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2412906263,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2413430218","pull_request_review_id":3314216682,"id":2413430218,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6P2gXK","diff_hunk":"@@ -809,7 +809,10 @@\n \t\t<constant name=\"CLIP_CHILDREN_AND_DRAW\" value=\"2\" enum=\"ClipChildrenMode\">\n \t\t\tThis node is used as a mask and is also drawn. The mask is based on this node's alpha channel: Opaque pixels are kept, transparent pixels are discarded, and semi-transparent pixels are blended in according to their opacity. Children are clipped to the parent's drawn area.\n \t\t</constant>\n-\t\t<constant name=\"CLIP_CHILDREN_MAX\" value=\"3\" enum=\"ClipChildrenMode\">\n+\t\t<constant name=\"CLIP_CHILDREN_CANVASGROUP\" value=\"3\" enum=\"ClipChildrenMode\">\n+\t\t\tThis node is used as a [CanvasGroup]. Child [CanvasItem] nodes are drawn as a single object and their color values are multiplied by this node's color values. Overlapping opaque pixels are kept, transparent pixels are discarded.","path":"doc/classes/CanvasItem.xml","commit_id":"34d2589a6788597e823ca753915de389c1217e7e","original_commit_id":"34d2589a6788597e823ca753915de389c1217e7e","user":{"login":"tsutsen","id":68827291,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4ODI3Mjkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68827291?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsutsen","html_url":"https://github.com/tsutsen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsutsen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsutsen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsutsen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsutsen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsutsen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsutsen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsutsen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsutsen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsutsen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> What about any color value between opaque and transparent?\r\n\r\nYes, this needs clarification. What about this? It follows the descriptions of other ClipChildrenModes closer:\r\n\r\nThis node is used as a mask and is also drawn in multiplicative blending mode. The mask is based on this node's alpha channel: Opaque pixels are kept, transparent pixels are discarded, and semi-transparent pixels are blended in according to their opacity. Children are drawn as a single object and clipped to the parent's drawn area.\r\n\r\nWe could also link the [blend mode docs](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_canvasitemmaterial.html#enum-canvasitemmaterial-blendmode) here.\r\n\r\nUPD: commited this description","crea